WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:06.327
Time passed, and Ellen grew up.

2
00:00:06.328 --> 00:00:09.398
She got used to keeping rocks in her pockets.

3
00:00:09.399 --> 00:00:13.258
This kept her from floating away.

4
00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:17.457
And her parents began to enjoy having a light princess.

5
00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:21.188
With Ellen, the palace always rang with laughter.

6
00:00:21.189 --> 00:00:27.100
Life was always fun!

7
00:00:27.101 --> 00:00:32.142
By the time Ellen was 17, her parents were uneasy again.

8
00:00:32.143 --> 00:00:35.514
Yes, Ellen delighted everyone with her laughter.

9
00:00:35.515 --> 00:00:41.687
But she laughed at everything—even things that were not funny.

10
00:00:41.688 --> 00:00:46.150
For instance, whenever the queen cried, Ellen giggled.

11
00:00:46.151 --> 00:00:53.853
"Hee-hee! Mama, you're squeezing water out of your cheeks again!"

12
00:00:53.854 --> 00:01:00.784
Whenever the king yelled, Ellen floated around him like a butterfly, grinning.

13
00:01:00.785 --> 00:01:07.299
"Make that mean face again, Papa! You look silly!"

14
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:10.465
Then one day something awkward happened.

15
00:01:10.466 --> 00:01:13.952
Ellen was crossing the lawn with two servants.

16
00:01:13.953 --> 00:01:17.681
They held her hands tightly.

17
00:01:17.682 --> 00:01:22.164
But when Ellen saw her father, she yanked one hand away.

18
00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:25.638
"Papa!"

19
00:01:25.639 --> 00:01:29.180
Ellen looked for rocks to put in her pockets.

20
00:01:29.181 --> 00:01:32.475
But all she saw was a big black toad.

21
00:01:32.476 --> 00:01:37.785
She grabbed it and started running.

22
00:01:37.786 --> 00:01:41.232
She held out her arms, ready to kiss her father.

23
00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:43.496
Suddenly there was a puff of wind.

24
00:01:43.497 --> 00:01:51.205
The princess flew in another direction—into a young page's arms. Smack!

25
00:01:51.206 --> 00:01:55.085
The princess planted a kiss on one of the page's cheeks.

26
00:01:55.086 --> 00:02:00.822
On the other cheek, she slapped him—with the huge black toad!

27
00:02:00.823 --> 00:02:06.715
The princess giggled. "I hope you like toads!"

28
00:02:06.716 --> 00:02:10.577
The king turned red as she shrieked with laughter.

29
00:02:10.578 --> 00:02:17.942
"This is so embarrassing!" he thought. "Something must be done."

30
00:02:17.943 --> 00:02:22.020
The next morning the king and queen sent for the princess.

31
00:02:22.021 --> 00:02:25.312
She had only a few small stones in her pockets.

32
00:02:25.313 --> 00:02:31.428
So it took her a while to sit down.

33
00:02:31.429 --> 00:02:34.441
The king cleared his throat.

34
00:02:34.442 --> 00:02:38.166
"Ellen, you know you're different from everyone."

35
00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:41.976
"No, I'm not!" Ellen laughed.

36
00:02:41.977 --> 00:02:48.485
"I have a nose, two eyes, and a mouth, like everyone else."

37
00:02:48.486 --> 00:02:52.292
"Be serious," her mother said.

38
00:02:52.293 --> 00:03:00.894
"No, thank you. I like being silly!"

39
00:03:00.895 --> 00:03:03.945
Ellen laughed and laughed.

40
00:03:03.946 --> 00:03:08.388
The king looked at his wife. "Now what?"

41
00:03:08.389 --> 00:03:11.671
"There's only one thing to do," she said.

42
00:03:11.672 --> 00:03:25.524
"We must send for Kopp and Humm—the kingdom's wisest philosophers."

